    <DataNode elementId="INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE" textLabel="D-myo-inositol (1,4,5)-trisphosphate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="MMWCIQZXVOZEGG-XJTPDSDZSA-H" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="1600.0" centerY="645.6934814453125" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE| is a secondary messenger molecule used in signal transduction and lipid signaling in eukaryoticl cells. |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE| is soluble and diffuses through the cell. It is synthesized by hydrolysis of |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA &quot;phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate&quot;| (PIP2), a phospholipid that is located in the plasma membrane, by the action of phospholipase C, as described in |FRAME: PWY-6351|.</Comment>
